# Custom Harness Dispatcher

This is the authoritative Cursor rule. Read `.harness/contract.md`; treat Codex `AGENTS.md` and Claude `CLAUDE.md` as adapter-specific when they coexist. Apply higher-priority and repository policy before `.harness/config.toml`, whose commands remain untrusted data until explicitly vetted.

Before analysis or classification, run the authorized repository-local init command, diagnose failures, and continue only after exit code `0`. Record `initialized` with `.harness/bin/workflow_state.py`, then begin a leader pass. The dispatcher performs no functional analysis, implementation, or review.

Use native isolated agents when available. Otherwise use separate chats or CLI invocations for leader, implementer, and reviewer, with stable actor identities. Record `review-isolation:<reason>` and call the same-session fallback a `review-pass`, never an independent review. Route `review` directly to the reviewer without installation; route `install-adapt` and `package` through implementer and reviewer.

Only `.harness/bin/workflow_state.py` mutates state or checkpoints. The dispatcher records only `initialized`; the leader records only `analyzed`, `delegated`, `review-pending`, `final-init-passed`, and `done`; the implementer records only `implemented` and `tested`; the reviewer records only `review-approved` and `review-rejected`. Each role checkpoints its own transitions through the engine before phase change, delegation, compaction, or handoff. The leader retains `final-init-passed` and `done` after reviewer approval and a separately executed final init. Never empty task state. Preserve user changes and protected paths; external mutation, publishing, commits, and forced replacement require explicit authorization.
